  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 1216 PM CDT Sat Aug 29 2026\n\nFairly similar conditions are expected Sunday through at least \nnext Saturday as upper level ridging meanders across the\nmidwest.\n\nPrecipitation: Little to none. 15-20% chances next Saturday.\n\nHeat: In general, areas NW of I-44 should see the higher end of\nthe temperature spectrum, but areas SE of I-44 will have higher\nhumidity, so impacts will overall be similar across the area. \nExpected Daily highs in the mid 90s to low 100s. Look for heat \nindex values of 100-105+. Heat Risk will be in the major to \nextreme categories. WBGT categories will be high to extreme. \nHeat headlines will likely be needed in the coming days. This is\nwell supported by the NBM, ensembles, and ensemble tools.\n\nFor additional context, average highs in Late August to early \nSeptember are in the mid 80s, so we will likely see temperatures\nof 10-15+ degrees above normal. Some records (see climate\nsection) may be broken, but the current forecast keeps \ntemperatures below records. \n\nHow long will the heat last? Ensemble guidance as CPC outlooks \nsuggest possibly into the middle of September. This will\ncontinue our rapid onset drought conditions.\n\nFire weather concerns Sunday: Hot and dry conditions (minimum RH\nof 25-35%) and S/SW winds of 10-15 mph gusting to 15-25 mph\n(strongest along/west of I-49) may lead to elevated grassfire \npotential.",
